[ti:One Player Too Many]
[ar:Mippithedork]
[offset:-400]

[00:01.77]Come on in, kid. 
[00:03.07]Pull you up a chair.
[00:05.93]I hear you're makin' yourself a video game.
[00:09.22]That's wonderful.
[00:11.90]Now tell me somethin'...
[00:13.56]You ain't plannin' on makin' it multiplayer, are ya?
[00:17.19]You say, 
[00:18.07]Well, actually...
[00:18.90]Oh, Lord.
[00:27.09]I knew a boy from Tennessee
[00:29.95]Made a platformer, just like me
[00:32.98]Had a little jump, 
[00:34.58]Had a little dash
[00:36.44]Had a little dream of makin' cash
[00:39.41]Then one fine day, 
[00:40.97]His buddy said
[00:42.30]"Let's put two players in instead!"
[00:45.56]Now his jump don't jump, 
[00:47.23]His dash don't dash
[00:48.82]And his server bill's eatin' all his cash
[00:52.29]One player jumps, 
[00:53.94]And all is fine
[00:55.53]Two players jump, 
[00:56.79]You bend space-time
[00:58.50]Three players join, 
[00:59.95]The world's on fire
[01:01.69]Four players crash the whole damn wire!
[01:04.86]Don't put multiplayer in that game, son!
[01:08.04]Don't go thinkin' it'll be more fun!
[01:11.29]You got one little player, 
[01:12.91]And he works just fine
[01:14.38]Now you wanna synchronize him 'cross space 'n time?
[01:17.65]You'll lose your sleep, 
[01:19.18]You'll lose your hair
[01:20.83]You'll debug ghosts that ain't even there
[01:23.84]You can make that game, 
[01:25.49]You can get it done
[01:27.27]Just don't put multiplayer in that game, son!
[01:33.83]I knew a gal with a racing game
[01:36.93]Single-player, smooth as a Cadillac frame
[01:40.37]Then she added online play
[01:43.37]And watched the cars just float away
[01:46.87]One car's here, 
[01:48.46]One car's there
[01:49.79]One's upside down and one ain't anywhere
[01:52.81]She said "I'll fix it with interpolation"
[01:56.10]Now they're driftin' through the fourth dimension!
[02:00.25]You say... 
[02:00.95]But what about rollback?
[02:02.85]Oh, honey...
[02:07.58]I knew a team with a sword and shield
[02:09.92]Built a hundred monsters in a field
[02:13.17]Then someone said "Let's play with friends!"
[02:16.33]That's where the happy story ends
[02:19.65]Now who gets loot? 
[02:21.36]And who gets gold?
[02:22.98]Who owns the quest when the host gets old?
[02:26.08]Who's in charge when the players split?
[02:29.37]And why's that goblin attacking itself?!
[02:32.81]The client says hit! 
[02:34.21]The server says miss!
[02:36.00]The player's screaming 
[02:37.22]"WHAT THE HELL IS THIS?"
[02:39.13]He swears he dodged, 
[02:40.56]The logs disagree
[02:42.23]And somebody's duplicated the currency!
[02:45.25]Don't put multiplayer in that game, son!
[02:48.44]Don't go thinkin' it'll be more fun!
[02:51.70]You got one little player, 
[02:53.32]And he works just fine
[02:54.64]Now you wanna synchronize him 'cross space 'n time?
[02:58.08]You'll lose your sleep, 
[02:59.69]You'll lose your hair
[03:01.16]You'll debug ghosts that ain't even there
[03:04.32]You can make that game, 
[03:06.00]You can get it done
[03:07.72]Just don't put multiplayer in that game, son!
[03:11.39]Now listen close, 
[03:12.86]I'll tell you true
[03:14.57]Multiplayer ain't just player two
[03:17.63]It's servers, bandwidth, fraud, and fees
[03:20.50]And players spread across seven seas
[03:24.01]It's lobbies, parties, matchmaking queues
[03:27.20]It's disconnects 
[03:28.68]And the rage-quit blues
[03:30.51]It's balancing powers for four or five
[03:34.00]And keeping an empty world alive
[03:37.83]And that's before somebody figures out how to cheat.
[03:40.44]But you say, I just want my friends to play together!
[03:43.72]So did the last twelve studios I buried...
[04:00.83]I knew a man, 
[04:01.90]He made a farm
[04:03.66]Had little chickens, 
[04:04.87]Had a great big barn
[04:06.93]He said "My wife could join me too!"
[04:09.84]Next thing you know, there's a chicken coup!
[04:12.68]The eggs got duped, 
[04:14.69]The cows desynced
[04:16.38]The crops rolled back, 
[04:17.89]The database blinked
[04:19.63]His wife logged out, 
[04:21.25]The world went black
[04:22.72]His chickens traveled three days back!
[04:26.26]Now he's got servers coast to coast
[04:29.36]A million chickens and a missing host
[04:32.55]And every time somebody plants a seed
[04:35.44]His backend starts to smoke and bleed!
[04:38.83]DON'T PUT MULTIPLAYER IN THAT GAME, SON!
[04:42.17]DON'T GO THINKIN' IT'LL BE MORE FUN!
[04:45.47]You got one little player, 
[04:47.31]And he works just fine
[04:48.58]Now you wanna synchronize him 'cross space 'n time?
[04:51.86]You'll lose your sleep, 
[04:53.41]You'll lose your hair
[04:55.03]You'll debug ghosts that ain't even there
[04:58.20]You can make that game, 
[04:59.95]You can get it done
[05:01.56]JUST DON'T PUT MULTIPLAYER 
[05:06.56]IN THAT GAME, SON!
[05:09.67]Now, I ain't sayin' multiplayer games ain't worth makin'.
[05:13.81]Some of the finest games ever made were multiplayer.
[05:17.29]I'm just sayin'...
[05:18.88]If you ain't ever made a game before, 
[05:21.62]Maybe don't start with the kind that needs 
[05:23.80]Four computers to agree on where a chicken is.
[05:28.29]Okay, 
[05:30.06]But what if it's an MMO?
[05:33.20]...Get out.
[05:37.81]... Get out.
